{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":204545,"duration_api_ms":201982,"num_turns":28,"result":"Perfect! I've successfully analyzed the 1000genome workflow and produced a comprehensive WDD YAML file. Here's the complete output:\n\n```yaml\nschema_version: wrd-7.0\n\nmetadata:\n  workflow_lineage_id: wrd:1000genome\n  version: 1.0.0\n  version_notes: Initial WDD compiled from static analysis of daxgen.py and task executables\n  deprecated: false\n  workflow_name: 1000Genome\n  workflow_description: >\n    A bioinformatics workflow analyzing human genetic variation from the 1000 Genomes\n    Project. The workflow identifies and characterizes mutational overlaps by chromosome\n    and population using SIFT scoring to assess variant impact. Tasks fetch, parse, and\n    cross-match SNP variants with functional predictions, producing statistical\n    distributions of mutation overlaps for disease association studies. The workflow\n    processes ~250k variants per chromosome across 2504 individuals in 26 populations,\n    enabling null distribution generation for rigorous statistical evaluation of\n    potential disease-related mutations.\n  source_repository: /home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflows_repo/1000genome-workflow\n  source_commit: null\n  source_format: pegasus-python-api\n\nstages:\n  - stage_id: stage:individuals\n    name: Individuals\n    description: >\n      Processes raw 1000 Genomes VCF files to extract individual-level mutation\n      data. Splits chromosome files into parallel chunks and creates per-individual\n      mutation records. Merges chunked results into single per-chromosome archive.\n    task_ids:\n      - task:individuals\n      - task:individuals_merge\n\n  - stage_id: stage:variant_filtering\n    name: Variant Filtering\n    description: >\n      Filters SNP variants using SIFT scores from Variant Effect Predictor data.\n      Selects only variants with SIFT predictions and creates indexed mapping.\n    task_ids:\n      - task:sifting\n\n  - stage_id: stage:analysis\n    name: Analysis\n    description: >\n      Analyzes mutation overlaps between individual pairs within populations and\n      computes frequency distributions of mutation co-occurrence patterns.\n    task_ids:\n      - task:mutation_overlap\n      - task:frequency\n\ntasks:\n  - task_id: task:individuals\n    name: Individuals\n    display_name: Extract Individual Mutations\n    stage: stage:individuals\n    executable: bin/individuals.py\n    description: >\n      Parses chromosome-level VCF files and extracts SNP variants for each individual.\n      Processes a subset of lines from the input VCF file, filtering by allele\n      frequency threshold and genotype status. Outputs per-individual mutation\n      files in a compressed archive.\n    behavioral_notes: >\n      Reads input VCF sequentially and writes per-individual output files\n      incrementally. Memory usage scales with input lines processed per job\n      (250,000 lines max; split into chunks via daxgen.py parameter).\n      Performs tar.gz compression at completion. Parallelizes via multiple\n      instances per chromosome (configured by -i flag in daxgen.py).\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: embarrassingly_parallel\n      description: >\n        Each instance processes a disjoint range of lines from the same VCF file.\n        No synchronization between instances; data is combined later by\n        individuals_merge task.\n    io_dominance: io_bound\n    io_access_type: python_serial\n    restart_model: idempotent\n\n  - task_id: task:individuals_merge\n    name: Individuals Merge\n    display_name: Merge Individual Data\n    stage: stage:individuals\n    executable: bin/individuals_merge.py\n    description: >\n      Merges individual mutation data from multiple chunked individuals tasks.\n      Decompresses tar archives, concatenates individual files, and re-archives.\n      Produces a single merged archive per chromosome ready for downstream analysis.\n    behavioral_notes: >\n      Reads multiple tar.gz files sequentially, extracts, merges file contents\n      (concatenates lines), and writes single archive. Uses temporary directory\n      to avoid holding all data in memory. Performs cleanup of temporary files.\n      I/O pattern is sequential streaming of text files.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: serial\n      description: >\n        One merge job per chromosome; merges all chunked outputs for that chromosome.\n        Runs after all parallel individuals instances for the chromosome complete.\n    io_dominance: io_bound\n    io_access_type: python_serial\n    restart_model: idempotent\n\n  - task_id: task:sifting\n    name: Sifting\n    display_name: Filter Variants by SIFT Score\n    stage: stage:variant_filtering\n    executable: bin/sifting.py\n    description: >\n      Filters SNP variants from Variant Effect Predictor output using SIFT scores.\n      Selects only variants marked as deleterious or tolerated and containing rs\n      identifiers. Extracts line numbers, variant IDs, ENSG identifiers, and SIFT\n      predictions into a structured output file per chromosome.\n    behavioral_notes: >\n      Reads entire input VCF file to extract headers and filter lines matching\n      SIFT patterns (subprocess grep), then re-reads filtered results to parse\n      and format. Writes single output file with tab-separated records. Uses\n      regex filtering and line-by-line parsing.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: serial\n      description: >\n        One sifting task per chromosome. No parallelism; operates on chromosome\n        VEP file independently.\n    io_dominance: io_bound\n    io_access_type: python_serial\n    restart_model: idempotent\n\n  - task_id: task:mutation_overlap\n    name: Mutation Overlap\n    display_name: Compute Pairwise Mutation Overlap\n    stage: stage:analysis\n    executable: bin/mutation_overlap.py\n    description: >\n      Analyzes mutational overlap between individual pairs within a population\n      and chromosome. Extracts individual mutation sets, computes all pairwise\n      intersections, and generates overlap matrices. Produces visualization plots\n      and quantitative overlap distributions.\n    behavioral_notes: >\n      Loads merged individual tar archive into memory, reads population roster,\n      reads SIFT-filtered variants, and computes all-pairs mutation intersections\n      using nested loops. Uses numpy for matrix operations. Generates PNG plots\n      incrementally. Outputs tar archive containing matrices and plots at end.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: embarrassingly_parallel\n      description: >\n        One task per chromosome-population combination. Tasks are independent;\n        parallelism achieved through multiple task submissions.\n    io_dominance: compute_bound\n    io_access_type: python_serial\n    restart_model: idempotent\n\n  - task_id: task:frequency\n    name: Frequency\n    display_name: Compute Mutation Frequency\n    stage: stage:analysis\n    executable: bin/frequency.py\n    description: >\n      Analyzes frequency of mutation overlaps by sampling random individual sets\n      and computing mutation co-occurrence distributions. Runs 1000 sampling trials\n      to generate a null distribution of overlap frequencies for each chromosome\n      and population.\n    behavioral_notes: >\n      Loads individual data and repeatedly samples random subsets, computing\n      mutation overlaps and histograms. Uses numpy for statistical calculations.\n      Generates multiple PNG plots (1000 plots per run). Outputs tar archive\n      containing frequency distributions and plots.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: embarrassingly_parallel\n      description: >\n        One task per chromosome-population combination. Internal loop runs\n        1000 iterations (n_runs parameter).\n    io_dominance: compute_bound\n    io_access_type: python_serial\n    restart_model: idempotent\n\ndata_objects:\n  - data_id: data:chromosome_vcf\n    name: Chromosome VCF\n    description: >\n      Raw VCF (Variant Call Format) files from 1000 Genomes Phase3 release.\n      Contains genotype information for all individuals at all SNP positions.\n      Approximately 250,000 variant records per chromosome.\n    format: text/vcf\n    cardinality: one_per_chromosome\n    lifecycle_stage: input\n    size_hint: \"500–800 MB per file\"\n\n  - data_id: data:columns_manifest\n    name: Columns Manifest\n    description: >\n      Tab-separated file listing all individual sample IDs in the same order\n      as VCF columns.\n    format: text/plain\n    cardinality: singleton\n    lifecycle_stage: input\n    size_hint: \"<1 MB\"\n\n  - data_id: data:vep_annotation\n    name: VEP Annotation\n    description: >\n      Variant Effect Predictor output containing functional predictions\n      (SIFT scores, phenotype, ENSG IDs) for variants.\n    format: text/vcf\n    cardinality: one_per_chromosome\n    lifecycle_stage: input\n    size_hint: \"200–400 MB per file\"\n\n  - data_id: data:population_roster\n    name: Population Roster\n    description: >\n      Text file listing individual IDs belonging to a specific population\n      (AFR, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS, ALL).\n    format: text/plain\n    cardinality: one_per_population\n    lifecycle_stage: input\n    size_hint: \"<1 MB per file\"\n\n  - data_id: data:individual_mutations_chunk\n    name: Individual Mutations Chunk\n    description: >\n      Tar.gz archive containing per-individual mutation files extracted from\n      a chunk of a chromosome VCF. One file per individual with mutation IDs.\n      Produced by individuals task.\n    format: application/gzip\n    cardinality: multiple_per_chromosome\n    lifecycle_stage: intermediate\n    size_hint: \"10–100 MB per archive\"\n\n  - data_id: data:individual_mutations_merged\n    name: Individual Mutations Merged\n    description: >\n      Tar.gz archive containing per-individual mutation files for entire chromosome.\n      Merged from multiple chunks by individuals_merge task.\n    format: application/gzip\n    cardinality: one_per_chromosome\n    lifecycle_stage: intermediate\n    size_hint: \"100–500 MB per archive\"\n\n  - data_id: data:sifted_variants\n    name: SIFT-Filtered Variants\n    description: >\n      Tab-separated file containing line number, rs ID, ENSG ID, SIFT prediction,\n      and phenotype for variants passing SIFT filter. Per chromosome.\n    format: text/plain\n    cardinality: one_per_chromosome\n    lifecycle_stage: intermediate\n    size_hint: \"10–50 MB per file\"\n\n  - data_id: data:mutation_overlap_output\n    name: Mutation Overlap Output\n    description: >\n      Analysis output for a chromosome-population combination. Tar.gz archive\n      containing overlap matrices, pairwise statistics, and visualization plots.\n    format: application/gzip\n    cardinality: one_per_chr_population\n    lifecycle_stage: output\n    size_hint: \"1–10 MB per archive\"\n\n  - data_id: data:frequency_analysis_output\n    name: Frequency Analysis Output\n    description: >\n      Frequency analysis results for a chromosome-population combination. Tar.gz\n      archive containing frequency distributions from 1000 Monte Carlo trials and\n      associated PNG plots.\n    format: application/gzip\n    cardinality: one_per_chr_population\n    lifecycle_stage: output\n    size_hint: \"5–20 MB per archive\"\n\npc_edges:\n  - pc_id: pc:individuals->individuals_merge:n_to_1\n    producer: task:individuals\n    consumer: task:individuals_merge\n    data_passed: data:individual_mutations_chunk\n    cardinality_pattern: n_to_1\n    coupling: tight\n    data_dependency: true\n    reasoning: >\n      All chunked outputs from parallel individuals tasks for a chromosome\n      must be collected and merged before mutation overlap analysis can begin.\n      Tight coupling: merge job waits for all chunks of chromosome.\n\n  - pc_id: pc:individuals_merge->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\n    producer: task:individuals_merge\n    consumer: task:mutation_overlap\n    data_passed: data:individual_mutations_merged\n    cardinality_pattern: 1_to_n\n    coupling: tight\n    data_dependency: true\n    reasoning: >\n      Merged individual mutations are read by both mutation_overlap and frequency\n      tasks for the same chromosome-population combination. One merged archive\n      serves multiple analysis tasks.\n\n  - pc_id: pc:individuals_merge->frequency:1_to_n\n    producer: task:individuals_merge\n    consumer: task:frequency\n    data_passed: data:individual_mutations_merged\n    cardinality_pattern: 1_to_n\n    coupling: tight\n    data_dependency: true\n    reasoning: >\n      Frequency task requires the same merged individual mutations as\n      mutation_overlap. Reuses the individuals_merge output.\n\n  - pc_id: pc:sifting->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\n    producer: task:sifting\n    consumer: task:mutation_overlap\n    data_passed: data:sifted_variants\n    cardinality_pattern: 1_to_n\n    coupling: tight\n    data_dependency: true\n    reasoning: >\n      SIFT-filtered variants are consumed by mutation_overlap (and frequency).\n      One sifting output per chromosome serves multiple population analyses.\n\n  - pc_id: pc:sifting->frequency:1_to_n\n    producer: task:sifting\n    consumer: task:frequency\n    data_passed: data:sifted_variants\n    cardinality_pattern: 1_to_n\n    coupling: tight\n    data_dependency: true\n    reasoning: >\n      Frequency task also requires sifted variants to compute overlaps without\n      SIFT filtering (within its own algorithm).\n\nworkflow_graph:\n  topology: dag\n  entry_tasks:\n    - task:individuals\n    - task:sifting\n  exit_tasks:\n    - task:mutation_overlap\n    - task:frequency\n  critical_path_estimate: >\n    individuals (parallel chunks per chromosome) → individuals_merge →\n    mutation_overlap / frequency (parallel across populations).\n    Sifting runs in parallel with individuals/merge path.\n\nworkflow_patterns:\n  - pattern_id: pattern:chromosome_parallel\n    pattern_type: parameter_sweep\n    description: >\n      Workflow is instantiated once per chromosome (typically 22 chromosomes).\n      All tasks are parameterized by chromosome identifier.\n\n  - pattern_id: pattern:population_parallel\n    pattern_type: parameter_sweep\n    description: >\n      Mutation_overlap and frequency tasks are instantiated once per population\n      (6 + 1 populations) within each chromosome. These tasks are independent\n      and can run in parallel.\n\n  - pattern_id: pattern:individual_chunk_parallel\n    pattern_type: data_parallel\n    description: >\n      Individuals task splits each chromosome into chunks (parameter -i in daxgen.py).\n      Each chunk is processed independently, then merged. Provides fan-out/fan-in\n      parallelism pattern.\n\nio_behavioral_hints:\n  - hint_id: hint:individuals_tar_overhead\n    task_id: task:individuals\n    potential_concern: small_file_overhead\n    description: >\n      Individuals task creates many small per-individual files (one per of ~2500\n      individuals) and immediately compresses them into tar.gz. Small file creation\n      and aggregation may incur filesystem metadata overhead.\n    severity: medium\n\n  - hint_id: hint:merge_tar_expansion\n    task_id: task:individuals_merge\n    potential_concern: temporary_expansion\n    description: >\n      Merge task extracts tar archives into temporary directory, concatenates\n      files, and re-archives. Temporary expansion can exceed archive size if\n      multiple tar files are extracted simultaneously.\n    severity: medium\n\n  - hint_id: hint:sifting_grep_pattern\n    task_id: task:sifting\n    potential_concern: format_conversion\n    description: >\n      Sifting filters large VEP VCF files using subprocess.grep with regex\n      patterns, then re-reads filtered results for parsing. Two-pass I/O over\n      large file may cause unnecessary disk traffic.\n    severity: low\n\n  - hint_id: hint:numpy_memory_load\n    task_id: task:mutation_overlap\n    potential_concern: memory_footprint\n    description: >\n      Mutation_overlap and frequency load all individual mutations and compute\n      all-pairs overlap matrices (NxN, where N is number of individuals per\n      population). Memory footprint may exceed available RAM for large populations.\n      No streaming/chunked computation observed.\n    severity: high\n\n  - hint_id: hint:analysis_archive_fragmentation\n    task_id: task:mutation_overlap\n    potential_concern: output_fragmentation\n    description: >\n      Analysis tasks produce tar archives containing many individual output files\n      (plots, matrices, distributions). Extracting or accessing subsets requires\n      full tar decompression.\n    severity: low\n\nexecution_profiles:\n  - profile_id: profile:local_serial\n    name: Local Serial\n    description: >\n      Single-machine execution using HTCondor condorpool backend. All tasks\n      run serially or in limited parallelism. Suitable for development and\n      small-scale runs (single chromosome, limited populations).\n    scheduler: condorpool\n    required_task_sets:\n      - all_tasks\n    parallelism_config:\n      max_parallel_individuals: 1\n      max_parallel_populations: 1\n\n  - profile_id: profile:hpc_parallel\n    name: HPC Parallel\n    description: >\n      HPC cluster execution (e.g., NERSC Cori) using SLURM scheduler.\n      Maximizes parallelism across chromosome chunks and populations.\n      Individuals tasks run in parallel per chromosome; analysis tasks\n      run in parallel across populations.\n    scheduler: slurm\n    required_task_sets:\n      - all_tasks\n    parallelism_config:\n      max_parallel_individuals: 250\n      max_parallel_populations: 7\n\n  - profile_id: profile:in_memory_aggregation\n    name: In-Memory Aggregation (Decaf)\n    description: >\n      Optional Decaf in-memory aggregation for accelerating individuals and\n      merge tasks. Requires --decaf flag in daxgen.py. Caches individual data\n      in distributed memory instead of tar archives.\n    scheduler: slurm\n    required_task_sets:\n      - task:individuals\n      - task:individuals_merge\n    parallelism_config:\n      max_parallel_individuals: 250\n\n  - profile_id: profile:mpi_cluster_mode\n    name: MPI Cluster Mode (PMC)\n    description: >\n      Optional Pegasus MPI Cluster mode for aggregating individual tasks\n      using MPI wrapper. Requires --pmc flag in daxgen.py. Reduces job\n      submission overhead for many small tasks.\n    scheduler: slurm\n    required_task_sets:\n      - task:individuals\n      - task:individuals_merge\n    parallelism_config:\n      max_parallel_individuals: 250\n\ntranslation_metadata:\n  generated_by: Claude Haiku 4.5\n  analysis_date: \"2026-03-11\"\n  analysis_method: static_source_code_analysis\n  confidence_notes: >\n    WDD generated via static analysis of daxgen.py (Pegasus workflow definition),\n    README, and task executables (Python scripts). All task dependencies,\n    data objects, and I/O patterns inferred from code. No runtime profiling\n    or execution traces were used. Task parallelism estimates based on observed\n    loop structures and daxgen.py job instantiation logic.\n  field_confidence_records:\n    - field: tasks[*].behavioral_notes\n      confidence: high\n      notes: Extracted from detailed code inspection of all task executables\n\n    - field: tasks[*].io_dominance\n      confidence: medium\n      notes: >\n        Estimated from I/O to compute operation ratio in code. Some tasks\n        (mutation_overlap, frequency) are compute-bound due to numpy matrix\n        operations, others are I/O-bound due to tar/file operations.\n\n    - field: io_behavioral_hints\n      confidence: medium\n      notes: >\n        Identified from code patterns: tar compression overhead, temporary\n        directory expansion in merge, subprocess grep in sifting, numpy matrix\n        allocation in analysis tasks.\n\n    - field: pc_edges[*].cardinality_pattern\n      confidence: high\n      notes: >\n        Extracted from daxgen.py workflow construction. Individuals chunks map\n        to one merge per chromosome (many-to-one); sifting/individuals_merge\n        outputs map to multiple analysis tasks (one-to-many).\n\n    - field: workflow_patterns\n      confidence: high\n      notes: >\n        Three parallelism patterns observed: chromosome-level sweep, population-level\n        sweep (independent analysis tasks), and individual-chunk data parallelism.\n```\n\nSTATUS: success | OUTPUT: /home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflow_wdd/1000genome-wdd-claude-trial2.yaml","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d62cb070-d7a8-476e-8dc6-f58e1baaf2b1","total_cost_usd":0.34119594999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":154,"cache_creation_input_tokens":83341,"cache_read_input_tokens":1312357,"output_tokens":21126,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":83341,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":154,"outputTokens":21126,"cacheReadInputTokens":1312357,"cacheCreationInputTokens":83341,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.34119594999999997,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"9ca638e7-2222-4655-8e89-5d6575d572be"}
